{
  "title": "Tutor \u2014 edtech (1,108\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Tutor\nDomain: edtech | Scale: large | Stars: 1,108\nProblem: Deploying, customizing, upgrading, and scaling Open edX platforms is complex and error-prone. Tutor provides a Docker-based distribution that simplifies the entire lifecycle of Open edX installations for both production and local development.\nTarget users: EdTech platform administrators, DevOps engineers managing Open edX, Developers building on Open edX, Educational institutions deploying Open edX, Non-technical users via zero-click AWS installation\nCore features: One-click installation and upgrades of Open edX via CLI; Docker-based containerized deployment for local and production environments; Kubernetes support for scalable deployments; Plugin/extensible architecture for customization; Built-in HTTPS/SSL certificate management; Zero-click AWS image deployment; Custom theming and translations support; SCORM xBlock and mobile app integration\nIntegrations: Docker, Docker Compose, Kubernetes, AWS, Open edX (edx-platform), PyPI, Let's Encrypt (HTTPS)\nTech stack: Python (CLI tooling) + Docker, Docker Compose, Kubernetes\nKey libraries: Click (CLI framework), Jinja2 (templating), Hatchling (build system)\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- CLI-first design pattern using Python Click enables both scripted automation and interactive use without a web UI layer\n- Jinja2 templating is used extensively for generating Docker Compose, Kubernetes manifests, and config files, enabling flexible environment-specific customization\n- Plugin architecture decouples core functionality from optional features, allowing community extensions without modifying the core codebase\n- Dynamic dependency resolution via custom Hatch build hooks (hatch_build.py) allows the package to conditionally bundle plugin requirements at build time",
